<title>RUSSIA: Russian Duma rejects T-bill, share tax.</title>
<headline>Russian Duma rejects T-bill, share tax.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's State Duma lower house of parliament rejected on Wednesday government proposals for a 15 percent tax on profits from share deals.</p>
<p>The tax would have been levied on institutions.</p>
<p>Deputies also rejected a draft law which would have removed tax exemptions on proceeds from trading government securities.</p>
<p>Some economists had warned that the tax would merely lead to a rise in yields on Treasury bills and raise government borrowing costs.</p>
<p>The average yield at an auction of six-month T-bills fell on Wednesday to a record low 49.63 percent from 65.98 percent on October 2.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
